    <briefdescription>
<para>Epoch-based fencing manager. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Maintains the authoritative current epoch for a shard and exposes a single check-and-fence entry point used by the Raft leader and all write-path hot spots.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Epoch Increment Protocol</heading>
</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>A new Raft term begins (or leader election completes).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The elected leader calls <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_epoch_fencing_manager_1af7a53b74e2f505dac84902842037acd3" kindref="member">bumpEpoch()</ref></computeroutput>, which atomically increments the counter and returns the new <ref refid="structthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_epoch_token" kindref="compound">EpochToken</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The leader attaches the token to every subsequent write RPC.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Followers call <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_epoch_fencing_manager_1af6f1f666a9b67770f7dc1e231d20fe07" kindref="member">checkToken()</ref></computeroutput> on every incoming write RPC.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If the token&apos;s epoch is stale, <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_epoch_fencing_manager_1af6f1f666a9b67770f7dc1e231d20fe07" kindref="member">checkToken()</ref></computeroutput> returns STALE_EPOCH and — if <computeroutput>auto_stonith</computeroutput> is set — triggers STONITH via the provider.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>This class is entirely in-process. Across processes the epoch is propagated through the Raft log; each node reconstructs it on replay. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
